==English==
[[Image:Backstroke (PSF).png|thumb|300px|the '''backstroke''']]

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|back|stroke}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{wikipedia}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbækˌstɹoʊk/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-backstroke.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[backhanded]] [[stroke]] or [[blow]].
#*'''1755''', {{w|Tobias Smollett}}, translating Miguel de Cervantes, ''Don Quixote'', Volume 1, I.1:
#*:He observed that Cid Ruy-dias was an excellent knight; but not equal to the Lord of the Flaming-sword, who with one '''back-stroke''' {{transterm|es|revés}} had cut two fierce and monstrous giants through the middle.
# {{lb|en|swimming}} A [[stroke]] swum lying on one's [[back]], while rotating both [[arm]]s through the water as to [[propel]] the swimmer [[backwards]].
# {{lb|en|bellringing}} The [[pull]] on the [[tail]] of the [[rope]] that swings the [[bell]] through a full circle (compare [[handstroke]])

